  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Voucher Packet",
    "overview": "**Creative North Star: \"The Voucher Packet\"**\n\nEvery invoice is a paper voucher packet lying on a grey-green desk blotter: an invoice copy, a PO copy and a check sheet stapled behind a voucher cover, routed desk to desk on a salmon routing slip, then rubber-stamped. Surfaces are sheets of multipart form stock, never cards. Printed form furniture (labels, rules, corner boxes) is in drop-out teal; anything the system \"typed\" onto the form is carbon blue-violet mono; decisions are rubber-stamp ink.\n\nThe register is green-bar continuous-form paper with tractor-feed margins; batch totals sit on an adding-machine control tape with a torn right edge; the test batch is manila stock. Density is clerical: hairline rules, tight ruled cells, exact figures. The world refuses the white-card SaaS dashboard with stat tiles.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Paper stocks carry meaning: each packet copy has its own colored stock.",
      "Three inks with fixed jobs: teal prints the form, carbon fills it in, stamp inks decide.",
      "Square corners and hairline rules everywhere; depth only as paper lying on paper.",
      "The decision is a raster rubber-stamp impression, and its one authored motion is the strike."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Three Inks Rule",
